{"name":"Durango Blue","hex":"#566777","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Durango","blocks":[{"text":"Durango, officially the Free and Sovereign State of Durango, is one of the states which make up the 32 federal entities of Mexico, situated in the northwest portion of the country. With a population of 1,832,650, the eighth lowest of Mexico's states, Durango has Mexico's second-lowest population density, after Baja California Sur. The capital city, Victoria de Durango, is named after the first President of Mexico, Guadalupe Victoria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/R%C3%ADo%2C_Monta%C3%B1a%2C_Durango_%2816697897432%29.jpg/330px-R%C3%ADo%2C_Monta%C3%B1a%2C_Durango_%2816697897432%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Durango"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg/500px-Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg/1280px-Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg/500px-Barrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"View toward the canyon at the Mexiquillo nature reserve","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarrancas_en_parque_natural_mexiquillo.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg/500px-Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg/1280px-Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg/500px-Tortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Desert tortoise in the Mapimí Biosphere Reserve","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATortuga_del_bols%C3%B3n.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/El_Picacho_desde_la_entrada_-_panoramio.jpg/500px-El_Picacho_desde_la_entrada_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&